From 6bb34808b9065c096519516e51457f1f34519f58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:18:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] test(chexc): clause-only type arguments, checking-off
 identity, the implicit close()

'generics_clause_only_neg.cj' is the text's own example plus the variant that used to be paid at
the bound; '_ok.cj' pins that explicit arguments and ordinarily-inferred parameters stay legal.
'off_ignores_throws.cj' and 'xpkg_off_consumer.cj' pin the ruling in both directions -- a local
clause and a clause loaded from a checked dependency both read as clause-free with the feature
off. 'twr_close_demand.cj' and 'twr_close_neg.cj' pin the implicit close: caught by the try's own
clauses, reported when they do not cover it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../scopes/off_ignores_throws.cj              | 35 ++++++++++++++++
 .../scopes/twr_close_demand.cj                | 30 ++++++++++++++
 .../CheckedExceptions/scopes/twr_close_neg.cj | 30 ++++++++++++++
 .../serialization/xpkg_off_consumer.cj        | 23 +++++++++++
 .../types/generics_clause_only_neg.cj         | 34 ++++++++++++++++
 .../types/generics_clause_only_ok.cj          | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 192 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 testsuites/LLT/compiler/CheckedExceptions/scopes/off_ignores_throws.cj
 create mode 100644 testsuites/LLT/compiler/CheckedExceptions/scopes/twr_close_demand.cj
 create mode 100644 testsuites/LLT/compiler/CheckedExceptions/scopes/twr_close_neg.cj
 create mode 100644 testsuites/LLT/compiler/CheckedExceptions/serialization/xpkg_off_consumer.cj
